     6	## High-level API
     7	The API provides:
     8	- `createServer(options)` for in-process server.
     9	- `connect(url, options)` for client.
    10	- `new WebTransport(url, options)` as additive browser-shaped client facade.
    11	- Sessions expose datagrams (Promise send + async iterable receive) and streams (Node streams).
    12	
    13	All streams must use standard Node stream backpressure semantics (write() returns false + 'drain').
    14	
    15	## W3C facade parity status (current)
    16	Source of truth: `docs/PARITY_MATRIX.md` (W3C snapshot: `docs/w3c/w3c.github.io-2026-02-04.md`).
    17	
    18	- Implemented in facade:
    19	  - lifecycle (`ready`, `closed`, `draining`)
    20	  - datagram duplex shape (`readable`, `writable`, `createWritable`, `maxDatagramSize`)
    21	  - datagram send options (`sendOrder`, `sendGroup`) with ownership validation + deterministic scheduling
    22	  - stream creation/incoming stream surfaces
    23	  - stream send options (`sendOrder`, `sendGroup`) with deterministic scheduling
    24	  - browser-shaped stream control mapping (`writable.abort` -> reset, `readable.cancel` -> stopSending)
    25	  - static capability `supportsReliableOnly`
